\subsection{The Detach Degradation: BatchNorm Artifact or Gradient Flow Effect?}
\label{sec:why_detach}

Detach OCC falls 3.4\,pp below Vanilla despite identical architecture and forward computation to Full OCC. The auxiliary head's BatchNorm2d layers update running statistics at every forward pass regardless of gradient routing; with \texttt{stop\_gradient}, the encoder bears this statistical perturbation without compensating auxiliary gradients. This forward-pass interference makes Detach worse than Vanilla: the encoder absorbs the cost of the auxiliary pathway without receiving any training benefit.

A discriminating test---replacing BatchNorm2d with LayerNorm while keeping \texttt{stop\_gradient}---would isolate whether the Detach deficit is a BN artifact or a genuine gradient-flow effect. \textit{[Detach+LN results pending; see \texttt{scenario\_variants.tex} for pre-written scenario analyses.]}

